# Always commit, always push

Applies to every code or evidence change made in this repository.

1. **Commit before you finish.** Never leave a completed unit of work uncommitted. One logical change per commit,
   with a real message (scope + what changed). Do not stage unrelated files.
2. **Push before you report.** After committing, immediately run `git push origin main`, then `git fetch origin`
   and confirm `HEAD == origin/main` and a clean tree.
3. **Never force, never rewrite.** No `push --force`, no `commit --amend` on pushed commits, no rebase/rewrite of
   shared history, no silent stash or discard of unrelated work.
4. **If the network refuses**, retry a few times over a couple of minutes, then: keep the commits local, create a
   bundle backup (`git bundle create <path> main`), and state the exact blocker (error text, host/port, attempts)
   in the report. Never claim a push that did not happen.
5. Push parity is part of the result: a report that says the work landed must also say whether `origin/main` was
   updated, or why it could not be.

## Network note (this machine, verified 2026-11-13)

Direct GitHub access is blocked here (github.com:443 / :22 / ssh.github.com:443 all closed). A local proxy listens
on `127.0.0.1:10808` (HTTP + SOCKS5) and does reach GitHub. This repo therefore carries a scoped setting:

    git config --local "http.https://github.com.proxy" "socks5h://127.0.0.1:10808"

Use that scoped form (never a global proxy) so other hosts and repos stay direct. If a push still fails, test with
`curl.exe -x socks5h://127.0.0.1:10808 https://github.com` before touching any git state.
